#  Daily Planner

A minimal Chrome extension for building a daily habit. You keep one fixed list of tasks that repeats every day. When you finish **every** task on the list, that day counts as **1 day of work** and shows up as a heatmap square in [Portfolio Tracker](../portfolio-tracker) on your new tab page.

> This extension lives in the same repository as Portfolio Tracker and is designed to work alongside it. The planner works on its own too, but the heatmap needs the tracker.

## Features

- **Constant daily routine**: add your tasks once and they appear every day, unticked each morning.
- **All-or-nothing days**: a day counts only when every task is done. Add or untick a task and the day stops counting until it is complete again.
- **Task descriptions**: add an optional description under any task, and edit it later with ✎.
- **Quotes on hover**: save your own quotes and hover over the day title to see one. With several quotes, a random one is shown each time.
- **History view**: step back and forward through days with ‹ and ›. Past days keep the task list they had at the time, so changing your routine never rewrites history.
- **Tracker integration**: completed days appear as a "Daily Planner" heatmap with a 🔥 streak in Portfolio Tracker.
- **Private**: everything is stored locally in your browser. There is no account, server or analytics.

